    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.23.39</title>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:47:35 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22339</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.39</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Main: every git pond has a Main place, its own folder. ⌘N starts a thread there; "In: Main ▾" picks a stream instead, and if Main is busy you're offered a new stream.</li><li>New streams clone dependencies (node_modules, .venv, ignored .env files) from the pond with copy-on-write, so they take almost no extra disk.</li><li>Ponds shared with you carry the sharer's initials on their icon; the sidebar filter has Mine and Shared with me.</li><li>The pond dashboard no longer jumps: its status lives in one fixed line in the header, and an idle shared pond talks to the cloud far less.</li><li>Every update action (Install, Restart to update, Cancel, Try again) is quiet text, in the sidebar, the menu-bar panel and Settings.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.38</h4><ul><li>Chat tabs fit their name: the close button sits right after the title instead of at the far edge.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.37</h4><ul><li>A pond can be any folder, git or not. Chats run right in the folder; things that need version history (streams, changes, pull requests) step aside and say why, and "Turn on version history" in the pond's settings sets it up when you want it.</li><li>Clean up disk: a page (Settings › General, or a pond's menu) lists stream folders Squeak no longer tracks, stale worktrees and merged branches with their sizes. Safe items are ticked, anything with unsaved work never is, and folders go to the Trash.</li><li>Archiving a stream whose branch is merged offers to delete the branch.</li><li>Settings › Add-ons: an action spins and fails only on its own card, gives up after 15 seconds with a reason, Remove on Zoho Cliq really removes it, and add-ons that aren't in this build don't offer Add.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
